If a wall seems to disappear spontaneously, it is likely that a ghost is
occupying the square. If the wall is completely gone (i. e., you can step
on the square), it has been taken down by a monster. Look out for rock
moles or dwarves with pick-axes.

>Oh, and sometimes when I start NetHack it says, "Be careful, New Moon 
>tonight." This is VERY cool, but how does NetHack know that there is a 
>New Moon 

NetHack calculates the phase of the moon by itself. It uses the following
rationale (copied directly from the source):

 * moon period = 29.53058 days ~= 30, year = 365.2422 days
 * days moon phase advances on first day of year compared to preceding
year
 *	= 365.2422 - 12*29.53058 ~= 11
 * years in Metonic cycle (time until same phases fall on the same days
of
 *	the month) = 18.6 ~= 19
 * moon phase on first day of year (epact) ~= (11*(year%19) + 29) % 30
 *	(29 as initial condition)
 * current phase in days = first day phase + days elapsed in year
 * 6 moons ~= 177 days
 * 177 ~= 8 reported phases * 22
 * + 11/22 for rounding

